    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="23.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIAtr">VI Atr</ref> 23.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="23.1" corresp="#wit-d-incomplete">And s<hi rend="italic">anct</hi>e Eadwardes mæssedæg witan habbað gecoran, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> man freolsian sceal ofer eall Englaland on XV kl. Apr<hi rend="italic">i</hi>l<hi rend="italic">is</hi>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="23.1" corresp="#wit-k">[And sancte Eadwardes mæssedæg witan habbað gecoran þæt man freolsian sceal ofer eall Englaland on XV kl. Aprilis.] [D]</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-k">And the authorities have decided that St Edward's festival shall be celebrated throughout England on the 18th of March.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">(Und des heiligen Eadward [des Märtyrers] Fest haben die Witan entschieden, dass über ganz England am 18. März gefeiert werden soll. D)</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(And the witan have decided that the feast of St Edward [the Martyr] is to be celebrated throughout all England on 18 March. D)</ab>
        <note type="editorial">23.1 follows only in D, as in V Atr 16 and I Cn 17.1.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
